WEBVTT

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.760
Shoot first, ask questions later

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:34.240
Sumanai

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:35.720
Osokunatta

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:36.970
Nanimonodaa!?

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:38.410
Mate mate

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:41.120
Odorokasete warukatta

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.250
Saa, sono bussouna mono wo orosunda

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:48.190
Gomennasai AKARI

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:50.270
Kyuuni haittekurukara, tsui

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:52.650
OK! Mondai nai!

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:54.010
Kimi wa un ga ii

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:57.220
Mou sukoshi de hachi no su ni natteita tokoro sa

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:01.470
Yoseyo, joudan kitsui ze

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:05.250
Sate, korede zenin shuugou shitane

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:07.650
Shinsaku na wake da ga

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:13.460
nani wo suru ka ka-do de kimeyou to omou

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:20.070
Junbi wa iikai?

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:21.700
Erabunda AKARI

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:25.520
Sore ga wareware no unmei to naruwakeda

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:28.370
Tanonda wa yo, AKARI

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:33.360
Oi oi

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:37.070
Kyanpu nante joudan kitsui ze

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:40.780
Oh! megami wa anata ni mikata shinakattayoune

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:46.500
Shiroi akuma ga azawarau jiki ni arienaiyo. Nansensu

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:52.090
Somosomo, konna nonki na koto wo yatteiru hima wa naidarou?

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:54.670
Tashika ni AKARI no iu toori da

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:58.610
Chotto ohuzake ga sugite shimatta ka na

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:01.180
Akkarin! Akkarin!

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:02.370
Kita ka!

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:03.450
Minna, deban da!

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:05.040
Sekai no tame ni!

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:07.600
Ikuzo!

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:13.440
OK! Rettsu go!

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:20.450
Ready, go!

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:21.470
Yuru yurin rin rin rin rin!

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:22.970
Yuri yuran ran ran ran ran!

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:24.580
Gimme a high-five, high-five.

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:27.660
It’s another wonderful day.

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:28.640
Okay!

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:29.540
It’s time for lift off!

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:30.120
Nachuyachumi!
Yuru Yuri

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:30.740
Where are we going?

00:02:30.740 --> 00:02:32.540
We’re all going on a fun camping trip!
Yuru Yuri
Nachuyachumi!

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:33.480
What?!

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:35.150
Camping! Camping!

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:36.530
Wait for me!

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:41.260
mezamashi tokei ga rin ririn ririn
My alarm clock goes ring ring ring ring ring

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:45.850
chikoku shisou de ran raran raran
I’m really running late, gotta run run run run run

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:51.190
itsumo no michi isogabamaware
Take the usual route, don’t be so hasty.

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:56.440
wasure mono wa tabun getabako no ue
That thing you lost is probably on top of the shoe rack.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:57.280
1st Place
The Girl with the Silly Face

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:02.600
shyugyou no beru ga kin kokan kakan
The school bell goes king kong kang kong kang

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:06.870
houkago made wa kukku kukku ku
Until the lesson ends it’s kukku kukku kuu (snoring)

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:11.710
itsumo onnaji sore ga shiawase
Our days never change, we live in constant bliss.

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:16.730
sagashi mono wa tabun kokoni aru kara
What you’re looking for is probably here.

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:22.820
zutto zutto isshyoni aruite ikitai
Forever and ever, I want to follow you on your path.

00:03:22.820 --> 00:03:25.560
genki mantan egao sansan
Brimming with cheer, your smile’s the best.

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:28.260
yay yay yay yay ittsu orai
Yeah yeah yeah yeah it’s all right.

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:33.420
donna toki demo warai aetara
If we can always laugh together.

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:36.040
tenki kankan junbi bantan
The weather’s bright, preparations all right.

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:38.320
yay yay yay yay ittsu okke
Yay yay yay yay it’s OK.

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:43.650
hateshinai mirai e
Onward, to the boundless future,

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:49.620
te to te to te to te o tsunaide kou
hand in hand in hand in hand we go together.

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:20.780
It’s another hot day...

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:23.660
Oh, I know!

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:41.920
Why does it have to be so hot...

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:44.360
For goodness’ sake.

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:54.100
Strange... nobody’s here.

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:58.340
Didn’t Akari-chan head here before me?

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:08.840
Ugh... so hot...

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:11.330
I really wonder where she went.

00:05:14.050 --> 00:05:17.520
Well, I might as well make some barley tea.

00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:28.090
I can’t believe I forgot we were out of tea.

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:32.540
I was looking forward to drinking some ice cold tea...

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:38.100
Well, I shouldn’t limit myself to cold drinks just because it’s hot.

00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:44.420
That had me scared for a sec.

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:46.700
Great, now my skirt’s all wet.

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:48.640
What a drag.

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:50.880
I wonder if it’ll dry on its own...

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:51.950
Oh, Chinatsu-chan!

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:53.840
It’s another hot day, huh?

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:54.620
Yui-senpai!

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:59.330
I guess your class ended ear...

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:04.300
No! It’s not what it looks like!

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:07.300
No, it’s alright, Chinatsu-chan.

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:09.150
It just kinda caught me off guard...

00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:11.450
No, really! It’s not what you think!

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:12.600
Y-Yeah.

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:16.250
This is tea! Barley tea! I just spilled it is all!

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:17.650
Oh, is that it?

00:06:17.650 --> 00:06:19.000
Yes, it is!

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:21.250
Look, just try smelling it!

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:23.230
You’ll just get the scent of tea!

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:26.110
No, I think I’m alright. It’s alright.

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:33.440
Hey! What’s wrong?

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:36.160
I thought maybe you’ll hate me!

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:38.750
Don’t cry, Chinatsu-chan.

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:39.870
It’s alright.

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:47.200
Even if you <i>had</i>  wet yourself, I could never hate you for it.

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:51.250
Yui-senpai! I couldn’t be happier!

00:06:51.250 --> 00:06:52.740
I love you!

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:53.910
Thank you.

00:06:53.910 --> 00:06:56.450
In any case, let’s wipe it up.

00:06:58.340 --> 00:07:01.010
Whoa, did you get burned at all?

00:07:01.010 --> 00:07:01.900
Yes.

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:03.860
What? Where?! We gotta put ice on that!

00:07:04.350 --> 00:07:06.550
Right on my heart!

00:07:06.550 --> 00:07:09.320
Oh, that’s good. You’re OK then.

00:07:10.420 --> 00:07:13.480
If we just put it here, it’ll be dry in no time.

00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:15.800
How about we hang up your uniform to dry too?

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:18.220
Oh, but I don’t have anything to change into...

00:07:18.220 --> 00:07:20.500
If you don’t mind my gym clothes, I can lend you those.

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:23.180
Your gym clothes?

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:26.250
I’ll wear it! I want to wear it!

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:29.210
Here, I’ll hold your skirt so it doesn’t get anything wet.

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:33.260
Yahoo! Make way for Kyouko-chan!

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:41.060
W-What perverted activity is this?!

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:42.950
I want in!

00:07:42.950 --> 00:07:45.700
You’re the only pervert here. Get a grip.

00:07:47.970 --> 00:07:51.240
Oh, so it was just a tea spill?

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:55.240
But are you <i>sure</i>  it was just tea?

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:58.050
What if you’re just using that as a cover-up?

00:07:58.050 --> 00:08:00.330
It’s the truth!

00:08:01.670 --> 00:08:03.930
Quit that. Stop teasing her.

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:06.910
It’s really hot today, huh?

00:08:06.940 --> 00:08:09.000
Oh. Akari, you’re later than usual today.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:12.250
I was wondering why your bag was here when you weren’t.

00:08:12.250 --> 00:08:16.720
I thought we could enjoy some ice-cream, so I went to get some.

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:17.890
Ice cream?!

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:19.550
How n<i>ice</i> of you, Akari!

00:08:19.550 --> 00:08:23.110
But I couldn’t find any rum raisin.

00:08:23.110 --> 00:08:26.490
Hah! Rum raisin has rum in it.

00:08:26.490 --> 00:08:29.020
Alcohol has a low melting point, which means rum melts faster.

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:30.830
Therefore during the high temperature of summer,

00:08:30.830 --> 00:08:33.410
storing rum raisin is more difficult, which is why it is winter only!

00:08:33.410 --> 00:08:36.570
Wow, I didn’t know!

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:38.060
Impressive.

00:08:38.060 --> 00:08:39.720
It’s nothing!

00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:42.260
Only when it comes to things you like, that is.

00:08:42.260 --> 00:08:43.910
What do you mean “only”?!

00:08:43.910 --> 00:08:49.620
Well instead, I got vanilla, and lemon sherbet, and...

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:51.680
What should I do?!
Look, see that?

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:53.800
That’s exactly how it happened!

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:55.860
Oh? Really?

00:08:55.860 --> 00:08:57.340
You’re lucky you didn’t get burned.

00:08:57.340 --> 00:09:00.080
Huh? What are you all talking about?

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:02.350
Oh no! The ice cream’s gonna melt! But then my skirt too!

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:05.500
Someone get some tissues!

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:07.920
We used them all up earlier.

00:09:09.820 --> 00:09:11.780
Toshinou

00:09:12.520 --> 00:09:14.780
It’s hot though.

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:17.740
That didn’t cool me down at all.

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:20.740
And I didn’t even win.

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:24.380
I wonder if we’ve got a fan or something.

00:09:25.300 --> 00:09:27.460
Maybe it’s in one of these boxes?

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:31.170
If we found a severed head we’d all be in cold shock.

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:33.130
That would be quite an incident.

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:36.420
Show-off

00:09:36.420 --> 00:09:39.160
It doesn’t look like there’s anything useful in here.
Show-off

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:40.510
Show-off

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:42.720
What’s this?

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:43.810
That’s a cooking kit.

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:45.180
It’s a pillow.

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:46.440
That’s a cooking kit.

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:47.730
It’s a bag.

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:49.860
Cooking kit.

00:09:49.860 --> 00:09:51.160
It’s a hat.

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:54.280
It’s a cooking kit!

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:58.960
I know! It was a joke, okay?

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:03.000
Oh really? Knowing you, I just assumed you were serious.

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:05.000
Duh! Obviously not.

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:07.280
What a shame. It’s empty.

00:10:07.280 --> 00:10:09.280
Is there supposed to be something inside?

00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:11.670
You’re usually supposed to find the last bit of hope inside.

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:13.670
What, is that supposed to be Pandora’s box?

00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:16.160
OK, put something in!

00:10:19.520 --> 00:10:20.010
Hot!

00:10:20.900 --> 00:10:23.140
I’d like to cook some rice.

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:26.280
You’re hungry?

00:10:26.280 --> 00:10:28.520
What, you’ve never been camping?

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:30.220
Of course I have!

00:10:30.220 --> 00:10:32.400
That’s when you set fire to things and watch ’em burn, right?

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:34.240
What kind of camping trip was <i>that</i> ?

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:36.600
We make a ring around the towering flames,

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:38.860
ceaselessly chanting even as our throats grow hoarse,

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:42.550
dancing until our bodies are depleted and our souls subsumed.

00:10:42.550 --> 00:10:44.960
What is this, some kind of occult ritual?

00:10:44.960 --> 00:10:46.120
Hey.

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:48.580
What might this be?

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:49.460
IT’S A CORPSE!

00:10:50.700 --> 00:10:52.380
Enough with the murder plots!

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:54.880
But it’s so hot...

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:58.740
Don’t scare me like that! Jeez!

00:11:00.980 --> 00:11:02.760
Oh, it’s a tent.

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:05.540
It looks like an antique.

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:08.350
Tents get you pretty excited, don’t you think?

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:10.350
I’ve got it! Let’s go camping!

00:11:10.350 --> 00:11:11.320
What?

00:11:11.320 --> 00:11:15.120
We’ve got a tent and a cooking set. That means we have to camp!

00:11:15.720 --> 00:11:18.110
What, we’re going to do a tribal dance around a towering flame?

00:11:18.110 --> 00:11:21.420
What is this, some kind of occult ritual? You’re scary.

00:11:21.420 --> 00:11:23.020
You said it!

00:11:23.020 --> 00:11:25.740
Let me explain to you what I mean by “camping”!

00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:27.200
And that is?

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:29.200
To be in nature and to meet nature.

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:31.040
At times, facing nature.

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:33.160
At times, savoring nature.

00:11:33.160 --> 00:11:34.540
And enjoying nature through it all!

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:36.980
To be in nature,

00:11:36.980 --> 00:11:38.980
and to meet nature…

00:11:38.980 --> 00:11:41.220
At times, facing nature!

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:43.940
At times, savoring nature.

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:47.490
And enjoying nature through it all.

00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:51.850
Well…

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:54.000
TOSHINOU KYOUKO!

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:55.360
Excuse us.

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:56.800
Oh, Ayano.

00:11:56.800 --> 00:12:00.320
Before you start your summer vacation, you need to turn in your paper!

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:03.050
Oh, sorry, I completely forgot!

00:12:03.050 --> 00:12:05.140
I was so busy with camping preparations.

00:12:05.140 --> 00:12:06.900
Camping preparations?

00:12:06.900 --> 00:12:09.200
Um, we are going camping, right?

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:11.980
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:12:11.980 --> 00:12:13.080
You’re all going together?

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:15.280
Approved! I approve this motion!

00:12:15.280 --> 00:12:16.500
Huh? When?

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:22.140
Hold on, you mean camping as in… you’re going to stay overnight?

00:12:22.140 --> 00:12:23.460
Yup!

00:12:23.460 --> 00:12:27.520
What? All of you, staying outside for the night?

00:12:27.520 --> 00:12:29.080
Oh, it sounds like fun!

00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:31.050
My <i>sediments</i>  are a Cambrian mountain range away!

00:12:31.050 --> 00:12:33.080
So you two will be coming with us then, right?

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:38.400
Um… it’s not… I mean…

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:41.690
N-No way in Niagara would I want to go with you!

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:45.160
That was two in a row… That’s really quite something.

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:49.370
Just <i>sand</i>  your message right away and be <i>dune</i>  with it.

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:54.540
Why won’t you laugh when I make a pun?!

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:57.080
There’s no need to restrain yourself, Yui!

00:13:05.980 --> 00:13:07.640
Mommy!

00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:09.640
Hurry! Quickly!

00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:12.920
The Mirakurun movie’s gonna start!

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:16.100
Don’t get too excited, Mari-chan. You’ll trip.

00:13:25.540 --> 00:13:27.940
<i>Being at a café on my own... it’s like I’m an adult.</i>

00:13:27.940 --> 00:13:30.370
<i>I was looking forward to it, a little.</i>

00:13:33.740 --> 00:13:35.250
<i>How wonderful.</i>

00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:39.330
<i>I wanna be able to sip from my drink as elegantly as that someday.</i>

00:13:40.520 --> 00:13:42.680
<i>Today, I just have banana juice though.</i>

00:13:45.840 --> 00:13:48.380
W-What are you doing, Sakurako-chan?!

00:13:48.380 --> 00:13:52.220
Well, I was walking with Himawari and I saw you!

00:13:52.220 --> 00:13:54.420
May we sit with you?

00:13:54.420 --> 00:13:56.020
Of course!

00:13:59.680 --> 00:14:01.660
Are we ready to order?

00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:07.640
Hey! This “Wiener Melange” coffee sounds like a good deal!

00:14:07.640 --> 00:14:10.060
It doesn’t come with a wiener.

00:14:10.060 --> 00:14:12.060
What? It doesn’t?!

00:14:12.060 --> 00:14:14.320
Fine, I’ll just have cocoa.

00:14:14.320 --> 00:14:16.220
Yes, and I’ll have it hot!

00:14:16.220 --> 00:14:19.400
And a hot lemon tea for me, if you please.

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:21.330
Yes, certainly.

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:26.240
You seemed a little fidgety about something. What is it?

00:14:26.700 --> 00:14:31.440
I was thinking, I wanna be like an adult who can look elegant enjoying a cup of tea.

00:14:31.440 --> 00:14:32.550
You’ve got practice, Sakurako-chan?

00:14:32.550 --> 00:14:34.420
Of course I do!

00:14:34.420 --> 00:14:36.260
Let me show you!

00:14:36.260 --> 00:14:38.080
Really?

00:14:38.080 --> 00:14:39.700
Alright, watch closely.

00:14:40.720 --> 00:14:41.660
Hot!

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:53.540
<i>She gave up…</i>

00:14:56.480 --> 00:14:57.500
Who is it?

00:14:58.260 --> 00:14:59.720
It’s Chinatsu-chan.

00:14:59.720 --> 00:15:01.720
She says she’ll be a bit late.

00:15:01.720 --> 00:15:04.130
Today, the two of us are going to study up on camping.

00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:05.860
Camping?

00:15:05.860 --> 00:15:07.960
The amusement club’s going camping!

00:15:07.960 --> 00:15:10.880
What? Really?! That sounds like fun!

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:13.540
So we’re going to read up on the subject.

00:15:13.540 --> 00:15:14.760
Give it here!

00:15:15.400 --> 00:15:16.980
This? Sure.

00:15:17.500 --> 00:15:20.020
So that’s why you’re studying.

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:21.960
Yeah, that’s right!

00:15:21.960 --> 00:15:24.160
OK! I replied that you’ll be waiting for her.

00:15:26.060 --> 00:15:27.280
Thank you!

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:30.400
<i>A reply? That was quick.</i>

00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:31.520
D
Chinatsu-chan
That’s quite bold of you,
Akari-chan…
I’m a little surprised （＾　＾；）
I’ll hurry so wait a
little longer!

00:15:31.520 --> 00:15:33.400
That’s quite bold of you, Akari-chan…

00:15:33.400 --> 00:15:34.660
I’m a little surprised.

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:36.200
I’ll hurry so wait a little longer!

00:15:37.940 --> 00:15:39.580
The cocoa’s a little cooler now.

00:15:40.340 --> 00:15:43.040
<i>What kind of reply did Sakurako-chan give?</i>

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:44.440
I’ll be waiting!
I’ll be waiting~!
It’s pretty hot today so I
just wore a swimsuit and
sandals♪（＞ワ＜🌼）
Gotta embrace the summer✩
Akari

00:15:44.440 --> 00:15:47.380
It’s pretty hot today so I just wore a swimsuit and sandals.

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:49.050
Gotta embrace the summer!
I’ll be waiting~!

00:15:49.050 --> 00:15:50.760
<i>That’s not embracing, that’s embarrassing!</i>

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:54.600
Come on, Sakurako-chan! You’re making me look weird!

00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:57.040
So sorry, it was just on an impulse.

00:15:57.040 --> 00:15:58.380
Jeez!

00:15:58.380 --> 00:16:01.020
Sakurako, there you go causing trouble again.

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:03.160
Alright, give it to me again then.

00:16:04.040 --> 00:16:05.580
Be serious this time, ’kay?

00:16:05.580 --> 00:16:06.900
OK. OK.

00:16:11.820 --> 00:16:14.200
The swimsuit was hot too so I took it off!
Chinatsu-chan
The swimsuit was hot too so
<u>I took it off!</u>

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:15.780
This is not OK!
Chinatsu-chan
The swimsuit was hot too so
<u>I took it off!</u>

00:16:15.780 --> 00:16:17.220
Jeez.

00:16:17.220 --> 00:16:18.480
It’s just a joke.

00:16:18.480 --> 00:16:20.980
You were definitely going to send it!

00:16:20.980 --> 00:16:22.740
Yeah, she was.

00:16:23.900 --> 00:16:25.400
Sorry for the wait!

00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:27.080
Wait, where’s the swimsuit?

00:16:27.080 --> 00:16:28.520
You believed it?!

00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:31.840
Sakurako was playing a prank.

00:16:31.840 --> 00:16:35.700
Oh, I see. I was thinking you were already in camp mode.

00:16:35.700 --> 00:16:38.820
No matter how excited I might be, a swimsuit is just not happening.

00:16:38.820 --> 00:16:42.520
All this excitement is enough to make Himawari want to suddenly change into a swimsuit.

00:16:42.520 --> 00:16:44.520
Not in the slightest.

00:16:54.120 --> 00:16:55.160
Now that’s improper!

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:58.840
What is the matter with you?!

00:16:58.840 --> 00:17:00.660
Himawari sure is unladylike.

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:09.360
...and that concludes the semester.

00:17:09.360 --> 00:17:11.710
Enjoy your break!

00:17:11.710 --> 00:17:13.670
THE PRINTS!

00:17:14.560 --> 00:17:17.420
Oh… it was a dream…

00:17:17.420 --> 00:17:19.540
What’s wrong?

00:17:19.540 --> 00:17:24.120
It’s just… like, it’s like that other room...

00:17:24.120 --> 00:17:26.320
Did you see a dream about camping?

00:17:26.320 --> 00:17:28.580
That’s right! Camping!

00:17:28.580 --> 00:17:32.120
Let’s go camping with Akari-chan and the rest!

00:17:32.120 --> 00:17:33.960
How did you know about that?

00:17:33.960 --> 00:17:37.120
We talked about it with them a few days ago.

00:17:37.120 --> 00:17:40.700
Yeah but… I mean, together…?

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:42.440
SUGIURA AYANO!

00:17:42.440 --> 00:17:44.000
Toshinou Kyouko?

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:45.740
I’m gonna borrow your AC.

00:17:45.740 --> 00:17:47.710
We are in the middle of a student council meeting!

00:17:48.360 --> 00:17:50.960
Yeah but it’s hot.

00:17:50.960 --> 00:17:53.200
Oh man, this is nice.

00:17:53.200 --> 00:17:55.740
It’s not fair that only you guys get this.

00:17:55.740 --> 00:17:57.740
Well, there’s not much I can do about that…

00:17:57.740 --> 00:17:59.680
Oh well, I’ll make do with some pudding.

00:17:59.680 --> 00:18:02.180
Hold it, what do you think you’re doing?

00:18:02.180 --> 00:18:04.840
I’ll take you camping, so just call it even.

00:18:04.840 --> 00:18:06.890
I don’t recall asking if I could go.

00:18:06.890 --> 00:18:08.890
Oh, camping sounds nice…

00:18:08.890 --> 00:18:11.150
Yeah, why not? Let’s go!

00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:13.940
It certainly does seem like fun.

00:18:13.940 --> 00:18:18.100
Getting bit by mosquitoes,
getting rained on, burning the rice…

00:18:18.100 --> 00:18:19.440
It really sounds nice.

00:18:19.440 --> 00:18:21.160
Those are <i>nice</i>  things?!

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:23.800
To share the burden of pain and suffering…

00:18:23.800 --> 00:18:26.260
It’s a recipe for romance!

00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:34.050
Don’t worry about me… just go on.

00:18:34.050 --> 00:18:37.640
No way! We’re going home together!

00:18:37.640 --> 00:18:39.510
We’re going back to Nanamori!

00:18:41.840 --> 00:18:42.970
Thank you...

00:18:42.970 --> 00:18:45.240
...so much...

00:18:45.240 --> 00:18:47.810
...for the fun…

00:18:49.270 --> 00:18:52.730
AYANO!

00:18:52.730 --> 00:18:55.730
Oh, the counter intuitiveness of it… so nice…

00:18:55.730 --> 00:18:58.480
You see? Everybody agrees it’ll be great!

00:18:58.480 --> 00:18:59.560
Let’s enjoy!

00:18:59.560 --> 00:19:00.450
Enjoy what?

00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:03.500
Oh! Me too! I want to enjoy!

00:19:03.500 --> 00:19:05.980
Look, Himawari will enjoy it too!

00:19:05.980 --> 00:19:09.120
Can you not make decisions for me?

00:19:09.120 --> 00:19:11.820
Not that I don’t agree.

00:19:11.820 --> 00:19:14.000
Let’s take a vote then.

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:15.740
I cast my vote yes!

00:19:15.740 --> 00:19:17.800
You’re not part of the student council!

00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:19.380
Come on, let’s go.

00:19:19.380 --> 00:19:21.550
Ayano, you really don’t want to go?

00:19:23.520 --> 00:19:25.300
Um, to say that I don’t want to go is…

00:19:25.300 --> 00:19:27.820
Well, that’s not quite it…

00:19:27.820 --> 00:19:31.270
How about we say I’ll do it if I have no choice!

00:19:31.270 --> 00:19:35.400
In that case, if you value the life of this little pudding, you’ll come!

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:36.580
Kidnapping?!

00:19:36.580 --> 00:19:38.880
No, this is pudding-napping.

00:19:39.920 --> 00:19:41.380
We’ll await you at the camping ground!

00:19:41.380 --> 00:19:42.490
Hey, hold on!

00:19:42.490 --> 00:19:46.330
Looks like we have to go!
That poor pudding’s life is in our hands!

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:50.320
Camping and pudding. It’s a dream come true!

00:19:50.320 --> 00:19:53.670
Yeah! That’s like… something in a dream!

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:56.860
She just said that…

00:19:56.860 --> 00:19:58.340
Alright, I get it.

00:19:58.340 --> 00:20:02.720
I’d be worried if it was just you guys out there, so we’ll join you.

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:04.720
Yeah! Camping confirmed!

00:20:04.720 --> 00:20:07.600
Yay! Campudding!

00:20:07.600 --> 00:20:08.460
Cool it, Sakurako!

00:20:08.460 --> 00:20:11.700
Can you please not hug me out of nowhere?!

00:20:14.080 --> 00:20:15.730
Camping sounds nice…

00:20:16.480 --> 00:20:18.580
I’ll be sure to bring home lots of stories.

00:20:18.580 --> 00:20:21.820
Kaede, once you get bigger, let’s go together.

00:20:22.660 --> 00:20:23.240
Okay!

00:20:23.900 --> 00:20:25.990
Yeah, so that’s what happened.

00:20:25.990 --> 00:20:29.740
I would’ve been fine with you staying there a bit longer though.

00:20:29.740 --> 00:20:31.740
Like for the rest of your life.

00:20:31.740 --> 00:20:33.710
What? My whole life?!

00:20:34.940 --> 00:20:36.540
You’re all going camping?

00:20:37.300 --> 00:20:38.250
It sounds like fun.

00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:40.250
It sure is!

00:20:40.480 --> 00:20:43.510
I’m so excited, I don’t know if I can go to sleep.

00:20:45.920 --> 00:20:47.260
Akari-chan is going too, right?

00:20:47.260 --> 00:20:50.560
Yes! And Yui-senpai too!

00:20:50.560 --> 00:20:56.100
In that case, Akari-chan’s sister will be at the house on her own, won’t she?

00:20:56.940 --> 00:20:57.900
I suppose.

00:20:57.900 --> 00:21:00.460
It must be lonely.

00:21:00.460 --> 00:21:03.860
I wonder if she’ll be alright. I’m worried.

00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:07.880
There we go.

00:21:27.470 --> 00:21:29.930
(North exit)
Koujo Park exit

00:21:34.580 --> 00:21:36.060
Yui-senpai!

00:21:37.220 --> 00:21:39.260
You’re early, Chinatsu-chan.

00:21:39.260 --> 00:21:40.520
You too, Yui-senpai!

00:21:41.150 --> 00:21:42.960
It’s exciting, isn’t it?

00:21:42.960 --> 00:21:43.520
Yeah.

00:21:43.520 --> 00:21:45.520
It’s really exciting, isn’t it?!

00:21:45.520 --> 00:21:47.960
You’re really enthusiastic about this, aren’t you?

00:21:47.960 --> 00:21:51.990
Yes! I’ve been so enthusiastic, in fact, that I made this!

00:21:52.800 --> 00:21:54.480
Wh-What is that...?

00:21:54.480 --> 00:21:55.960
It’s a charm to protect us from bears!

00:21:55.960 --> 00:21:57.830
And look! They match.

00:21:57.830 --> 00:21:59.820
T-Thanks…

00:21:59.820 --> 00:22:02.980
Now we’re all prepared in case we meet any bears!

00:22:02.980 --> 00:22:05.060
Made in Chiina, huh?

00:22:05.060 --> 00:22:06.040
Yes!

00:22:06.560 --> 00:22:07.840
Hello!

00:22:08.470 --> 00:22:10.470
What’s with the outfit?!

00:22:10.470 --> 00:22:13.600
What do you mean? I like this outfit.

00:22:13.600 --> 00:22:16.730
I hope you get stung. A lot.

00:22:16.730 --> 00:22:18.400
Just kidding!

00:22:18.400 --> 00:22:19.860
I am aware of the issue.

00:22:19.860 --> 00:22:22.260
So I brought something proper to wear too.

00:22:22.260 --> 00:22:25.110
This minimalist masterpiece!

00:22:25.110 --> 00:22:27.320
Get stung till you’re all bumps.

00:22:27.320 --> 00:22:28.610
All bumps?!

00:22:30.570 --> 00:22:32.760
Akari sure is late.

00:22:32.760 --> 00:22:35.540
That’s not typical of her, being late.

00:22:35.540 --> 00:22:36.940
Overslept, maybe?

00:22:36.940 --> 00:22:40.180
If we’re talking about Akari-chan, I don’t think so.

00:22:40.180 --> 00:22:41.680
Yeah.

00:22:41.680 --> 00:22:42.290
Alright.

00:22:43.520 --> 00:22:47.550
Having left home early enough to get here 30 minutes early,

00:22:47.550 --> 00:22:52.060
she came across an old lady carrying heavy stuff at a crossing.

00:22:52.060 --> 00:22:57.340
When she went to help, the old lady said she was going to visit her granddaughter, but got lost.

00:22:57.340 --> 00:23:01.000
So she helped her find the place using her hazy memory of the area, and thus ended up late.

00:23:01.000 --> 00:23:02.480
That’s way too cliché.

00:23:02.480 --> 00:23:04.190
Guys!

00:23:04.190 --> 00:23:05.480
I’m sorry!

00:23:05.480 --> 00:23:07.190
I left my house early enough so that I could—

00:23:07.190 --> 00:23:08.650
The old lady!

00:23:08.650 --> 00:23:11.740
What? How did you know?

00:23:13.620 --> 00:23:15.450
Alright, let’s go.

00:23:21.320 --> 00:23:23.540
It feels like it’s gonna get hot today too.

00:23:23.540 --> 00:23:27.040
If we’d done this earlier in the morning it would have been cooler.

00:23:27.040 --> 00:23:30.200
Kyouko-senpai was the one who decided on the schedule, right?

00:23:30.200 --> 00:23:31.180
It’s here!

00:23:36.960 --> 00:23:38.000
Hey.

00:23:38.000 --> 00:23:39.180
That is…

00:23:39.180 --> 00:23:43.900
Here it is! The special Mirakurun train is here!

00:23:43.900 --> 00:23:47.140
Wow! That’s cute!

00:23:47.620 --> 00:23:49.110
Chinatsu-chan!

00:23:49.110 --> 00:23:50.570
Here!

00:23:52.100 --> 00:23:54.320
Line up there!

00:23:54.320 --> 00:23:57.580
Jeez. Just for a little while.

00:23:57.580 --> 00:23:59.580
Hey! It’s Mirakurun and Mirakurun!

00:23:59.580 --> 00:24:02.200
So that’s why you chose this time.

00:24:02.200 --> 00:24:05.710
Okay, now get on. Wave at me from the window.

00:24:07.800 --> 00:24:09.590
Like this?

00:24:09.590 --> 00:24:13.400
Mirakurun on za mirakurun!

00:24:13.400 --> 00:24:16.850
But, could you try to have more of a <i>kyarurun</i>  feeling?

00:24:16.850 --> 00:24:19.020
Kyarurun?

00:24:19.020 --> 00:24:21.740
Yui and Akari are saying they want to see it too!

00:24:22.800 --> 00:24:24.580
Chinatsu-chan is cute.

00:24:25.260 --> 00:24:26.650
I understand.

00:24:26.650 --> 00:24:27.840
Um, I didn’t—

00:24:27.840 --> 00:24:29.110
Kyarurun!

00:24:29.110 --> 00:24:33.180
Kyarurun!
There it is! This is great!

00:24:33.740 --> 00:24:35.460
Anyway, let’s get on.

00:24:35.460 --> 00:24:36.780
Yeah!

00:24:37.920 --> 00:24:40.100
Thank you for riding with us.

00:24:40.100 --> 00:24:43.540
This is our initial stop.

00:24:43.540 --> 00:24:44.840
By the way, around this area—

00:24:44.840 --> 00:24:47.420
Oh, wow. Even the announcements are Mirakurun.

00:24:47.420 --> 00:24:49.980
They’ve really got it.

00:24:49.980 --> 00:24:52.400
It seems to be really popular.

00:24:52.400 --> 00:24:55.320
There’s a Mirakurun movie out right now.

00:24:56.430 --> 00:24:59.920
Then I wonder if this is all promotion for that?

00:25:03.940 --> 00:25:05.100
K-K-K-K-K-K-K-K-Ky—

00:25:13.360 --> 00:25:16.900
I thought I’d die there…

00:25:16.900 --> 00:25:20.280
Yui, you sure make a big deal out of things.

00:25:20.280 --> 00:25:21.920
Whose fault do you think that is?

00:25:21.920 --> 00:25:24.880
In any case, it’s good that we didn’t miss the train.

00:25:25.320 --> 00:25:27.960
We didn’t forget anything, did we?

00:25:27.960 --> 00:25:32.020
I don’t think so. I made sure to pack everything.

00:25:32.680 --> 00:25:36.180
Who is bringing the tent, again?

00:25:40.140 --> 00:25:41.510
TENT?!

00:25:41.510 --> 00:25:43.760
Not an issue!

00:25:43.760 --> 00:25:45.920
I arranged to have it express delivered.

00:25:45.920 --> 00:25:47.600
Delivered?!

00:25:47.600 --> 00:25:50.360
That is going to reach us, right?

00:25:50.360 --> 00:25:52.530
At the very worst, we can just sleep outside.

00:25:52.530 --> 00:25:53.650
No way!

00:25:53.650 --> 00:25:57.420
We humans are surprisingly durable, you know?

00:25:57.420 --> 00:26:03.320
As long as we have a little money, and big dreams, we can make do!

00:26:03.320 --> 00:26:05.960
You’re not going to distract from the issue with pretty words.

00:26:07.130 --> 00:26:08.670
Speaking of that, I’m hungry.

00:26:08.670 --> 00:26:11.240
What were you just saying?

00:26:12.660 --> 00:26:15.880
Speaking of that, that old lady gave me this as thanks.

00:26:23.000 --> 00:26:25.980
Speaking of that, we’re in the height of summer.

00:26:26.660 --> 00:26:29.520
Speaking of that, I made some sandwiches!

00:26:30.520 --> 00:26:35.150
The bear trinkets took up all my time, so I couldn’t make anything too great.

00:26:37.110 --> 00:26:39.600
Don’t expect too much…

00:26:44.820 --> 00:26:47.060
No… it’s nothing…

00:26:47.660 --> 00:26:49.460
It looks… tasty?

00:26:49.460 --> 00:26:52.170
Go ahead, help yourselves.

00:27:03.760 --> 00:27:05.010
Here we go…

00:27:10.270 --> 00:27:11.440
This is…!

00:27:11.440 --> 00:27:12.760
It’s good!

00:27:12.760 --> 00:27:13.230
Yeah.

00:27:13.230 --> 00:27:17.980
It’s delicious! It’s a miracle! It’s a Mirakurun sandwich!

00:27:17.980 --> 00:27:20.260
This isn’t tuna, is it?

00:27:20.260 --> 00:27:22.260
Oh, that’s mackerel.

00:27:22.260 --> 00:27:23.200
Mackerel?!

00:27:23.200 --> 00:27:26.460
I wanted to put more effort into it, really…

00:27:26.460 --> 00:27:30.240
No, I think this is a miraculous sandwich, honestly.

00:27:30.680 --> 00:27:32.670
Is it really that good?

00:27:32.670 --> 00:27:35.000
Yeah. It’s really good.

00:27:35.000 --> 00:27:36.750
You’re amazing, Chinatsu-chan!

00:27:36.750 --> 00:27:38.710
Mmph! Mmph!

00:27:38.710 --> 00:27:40.860
We have no idea what you’re saying.

00:27:42.080 --> 00:27:45.180
I’m glad I made them!

00:27:47.890 --> 00:27:51.350
I wonder what the camping spot is like? How exciting.

00:27:51.350 --> 00:27:52.460
Tonami Bus Stop

00:27:52.460 --> 00:27:56.100
It’s probably a place by a beautiful, snow-coated mountain range,

00:27:56.100 --> 00:27:58.360
its image reflected in a clear blue lake.

00:27:58.360 --> 00:28:01.340
Nearby there is a field where the flowers bloom wild.

00:28:01.340 --> 00:28:06.100
And in the distance, you can see a family of horses grazing. It’s gotta be like that!

00:28:06.100 --> 00:28:08.100
You really have high expectations.

00:28:08.620 --> 00:28:11.120
What kind of place are you hoping for, Yui-senpai?

00:28:11.120 --> 00:28:18.800
Well, I just wanna have nice weather,
with nobody getting hurt, and for us to be safe.

00:28:18.800 --> 00:28:21.740
Yeah, and I’d like the tent to arrive in one piece.

00:28:24.510 --> 00:28:26.900
I can’t eat any more!

00:28:26.900 --> 00:28:30.140
Yeah, you’re obviously not trying to change the subject.

00:28:30.140 --> 00:28:34.160
I just thought I might not get another chance to say something like that.

00:28:34.160 --> 00:28:35.150
Yeah, sure.

00:28:35.150 --> 00:28:39.650
I have a once-in-a-lifetime line I’d like to say too.

00:28:39.650 --> 00:28:41.460
What is it?

00:28:41.460 --> 00:28:43.280
Indeed, let’s hear it.

00:28:43.280 --> 00:28:47.380
Love is something you will never regret!
BEWARE
Keep all interaction with bears to a minimum.

00:28:47.380 --> 00:28:49.880
Wow! What sagely words!
BEWARE
Keep all interaction with bears to a minimum.

00:28:49.880 --> 00:28:51.980
That’s really like you, Chinatsu-chan.
BEWARE
Keep all interaction with bears to a minimum.

00:28:51.980 --> 00:28:52.000
BEWARE
That’s really like you, Chinatsu-chan.

00:28:52.580 --> 00:28:55.710
I have something to say too.

00:28:55.710 --> 00:29:00.520
What? You’re going to get married after this?

00:29:00.520 --> 00:29:01.670
No!

00:29:01.670 --> 00:29:06.760
I just want to say I’m so glad to be with you guys.

00:29:06.760 --> 00:29:09.120
Akari-chan sure is plain.

00:29:09.120 --> 00:29:10.760
Plainly cute.

00:29:10.760 --> 00:29:11.780
What?

00:29:11.780 --> 00:29:15.360
Come on, Akari. Plain is best.

00:29:16.400 --> 00:29:20.240
Alright! Break’s over, let’s go.

00:29:20.240 --> 00:29:21.230
Right!

00:29:26.980 --> 00:29:28.140
We have arrived!

00:29:29.640 --> 00:29:30.700
Wow!

00:29:36.500 --> 00:29:38.300
It looks wonderful.

00:29:39.400 --> 00:29:40.880
This is a nice place.

00:29:40.880 --> 00:29:44.420
More compliments! Keep ‘em coming!

00:29:44.420 --> 00:29:45.960
Yeah, good job.

00:29:46.460 --> 00:29:47.900
You’re late!

00:29:47.900 --> 00:29:49.850
Sorry!

00:29:51.100 --> 00:29:54.060
Well, I brought it for you. You’d better be thankful.

00:29:54.060 --> 00:29:56.480
This is the express delivery service you mentioned?

00:29:57.750 --> 00:30:01.120
It must have been a long ride for you. Did you take the bus?

00:30:01.120 --> 00:30:03.640
Yes! And you came by car?

00:30:03.640 --> 00:30:07.720
Yeah! We did stuff like play Sevens on the way, it was fun!

00:30:07.720 --> 00:30:09.100
You played Sevens?

00:30:09.100 --> 00:30:10.620
Yeah, we played some Karuta.

00:30:12.760 --> 00:30:13.660
Wow…

00:30:16.080 --> 00:30:17.870
Yeah.

00:30:17.870 --> 00:30:20.880
Alright, we’ll come get you tomorrow.

00:30:20.880 --> 00:30:22.600
Thank you very much.

00:30:26.500 --> 00:30:30.050
Sensei! Explode in moderation!

00:30:30.050 --> 00:30:33.390
I wonder if that’s the kind of thing you can do in moderation.

00:30:39.440 --> 00:30:41.540
There we go…

00:30:43.980 --> 00:30:45.840
Stop playing.

00:30:47.160 --> 00:30:48.110
You seem like you’re having fun.

00:30:48.110 --> 00:30:51.870
Because I get to work with you!

00:30:51.870 --> 00:30:53.910
This is a lot of work.

00:30:53.910 --> 00:30:56.540
Sakurako, could you hold that for me?
I’m getting bored of this.

00:30:56.540 --> 00:30:58.260
Sure!
You can say that once you’re done.

00:30:58.820 --> 00:31:00.450
Haha! It’s me, Pinocchio!

00:31:00.450 --> 00:31:02.540
There we go!

00:31:03.060 --> 00:31:03.880
Already?

00:31:06.960 --> 00:31:08.360
It’s done.

00:31:08.360 --> 00:31:10.360
This is pretty spacious.

00:31:11.020 --> 00:31:14.800
We’ve got some time. How about we take a walk around?

00:31:14.800 --> 00:31:16.180
Sounds good!

00:31:22.900 --> 00:31:25.980
The air is clean and refreshing.

00:31:25.980 --> 00:31:28.110
It makes my soul shine.

00:31:28.110 --> 00:31:31.600
So that means your soul was all dirty?

00:31:32.140 --> 00:31:35.420
It’s just a metaphor to say that it’s refreshing.

00:31:36.200 --> 00:31:38.080
There’s a see-saw!

00:31:38.080 --> 00:31:40.380
It’s decided! Yui, we’re getting on.

00:31:40.380 --> 00:31:43.640
What? I’d rather not. There’s probably a spider or something.

00:31:44.710 --> 00:31:48.540
In that case, it will have to be me and Himawari in your stead.

00:31:48.540 --> 00:31:51.240
Who are you trying to imitate?

00:31:51.240 --> 00:31:52.820
It’s exactly like you, isn’t it?

00:31:52.820 --> 00:31:56.100
The see-saw is kind of embarrassing, anyway.

00:31:56.900 --> 00:31:58.680
You’re wrong, Hima-chan.

00:31:58.680 --> 00:32:01.060
That’s a <i>gittan bakkon</i>.

00:32:01.060 --> 00:32:03.100
I haven’t heard someone call it that in forever.

00:32:03.100 --> 00:32:05.730
What? Isn’t it called a <i>gikkon battan </i>?

00:32:05.730 --> 00:32:08.610
I’m pretty sure it’s <i>gikkon batton</i>.

00:32:08.610 --> 00:32:09.990
<i>“Batton”</i> ?

00:32:09.990 --> 00:32:12.700
I say <i>gittan bakko</i>.

00:32:12.700 --> 00:32:14.840
There’s no <i>‘n’</i> at the end?

00:32:14.840 --> 00:32:15.740
Nope.

00:32:15.740 --> 00:32:19.720
Wait up a bit. I’m not following you guys.

00:32:19.720 --> 00:32:21.720
<i>Gitton</i> ? <i>Gitta</i> ?

00:32:21.720 --> 00:32:24.460
It’s true. It’s getting hard to remember.

00:32:24.460 --> 00:32:27.040
Let’s just call it a see-saw.

00:32:27.040 --> 00:32:29.040
You’re the one who started this.

00:32:33.510 --> 00:32:37.380
It must have been quite an ordeal to get here from the bus station.

00:32:37.780 --> 00:32:41.600
Yeah, it was kind of far so we took a break on the way.

00:32:41.600 --> 00:32:44.560
Kyouko-senpai was energetic the whole way, though.

00:32:44.560 --> 00:32:47.200
Yeah, that’s pretty much expected of Toshinou Kyouko.

00:32:47.200 --> 00:32:50.620
Toshinou-senpai! I want to snap, snap too!

00:32:50.620 --> 00:32:52.060
Sure.

00:32:52.060 --> 00:32:54.840
Yay! Thank you!

00:32:54.840 --> 00:32:56.940
Camera, camera!

00:32:56.940 --> 00:32:59.160
Funami-senpai, I’ll be going on ahead!

00:33:01.560 --> 00:33:02.820
Yui!

00:33:03.500 --> 00:33:05.560
W-What is it?!

00:33:07.600 --> 00:33:09.170
Oh, a spider.

00:33:09.980 --> 00:33:11.880
I saved you from a spidery fate.

00:33:11.880 --> 00:33:13.160
I get it, I get it! Just let go of me!

00:33:13.160 --> 00:33:15.560
Oh, this is camera gold. Get closer!
I get it, I get it! Just let go of me!

00:33:15.560 --> 00:33:17.420
Yui-chan! Did something happen?

00:33:17.420 --> 00:33:18.260
This is really cute!

00:33:18.260 --> 00:33:20.100
Nothing happened!

00:33:30.700 --> 00:33:34.840
Sakurako, can you get the curry ingredients that I asked for?

00:33:34.840 --> 00:33:35.820
Yes, ma’am!

00:33:36.640 --> 00:33:39.320
Sharing a meal with everyone is going to be fun.

00:33:39.320 --> 00:33:41.520
I’m hungry already.

00:33:41.820 --> 00:33:45.440
We did a lot of walking. I’m getting pretty hungry too.

00:33:45.440 --> 00:33:47.160
Then let’s make it quickly!

00:33:47.160 --> 00:33:49.170
I will give it my all!

00:33:50.060 --> 00:33:51.880
...remember: moderation.

00:33:54.520 --> 00:33:56.240
Here we are, Himawari.

00:33:59.430 --> 00:34:01.260
“Curry”...

00:34:02.140 --> 00:34:05.850
This is a limited edition, fairly hard-to-find brand!

00:34:05.850 --> 00:34:10.480
You were in charge of the meat too… right?

00:34:10.480 --> 00:34:12.320
Nothing gets past the ol’ Sakurako-sama.

00:34:12.320 --> 00:34:14.280
BONUS BEEF

00:34:19.680 --> 00:34:21.820
After an extensive survey,

00:34:21.820 --> 00:34:24.650
we’ve become aware of a crucial oversight in our food supply.

00:34:24.650 --> 00:34:27.520
As such, the following people will form our shopping team:

00:34:27.520 --> 00:34:29.340
Toshinou Kyouko-san.

00:34:29.780 --> 00:34:30.830
Here...

00:34:30.830 --> 00:34:33.120
Oomuro Sakurako-san.

00:34:33.120 --> 00:34:34.300
Roger Dodger!

00:34:34.300 --> 00:34:36.380
Yoshikawa Chinatsu-san.

00:34:36.380 --> 00:34:37.650
Here!

00:34:37.650 --> 00:34:41.020
Chinatsu-chan! Our dinner is depending on you!

00:34:41.020 --> 00:34:42.080
Yes!

00:34:44.260 --> 00:34:46.640
I want this! Let’s buy it!

00:34:46.640 --> 00:34:48.520
They have toasting mochi too!

00:34:48.520 --> 00:34:50.200
Which one do you want, Chinatsu-chan?

00:34:50.200 --> 00:34:51.360
Which one is it?

00:34:51.360 --> 00:34:53.380
Rejected and rejected.

00:34:54.480 --> 00:34:57.620
We’re going to quickly get the meat and the curry mix that we came for, and be on our way.

00:34:59.620 --> 00:35:01.220
What is it?

00:35:01.220 --> 00:35:05.220
Yui sure would love these potato chips.

00:35:06.160 --> 00:35:10.080
Funami-senpai probably wants some baked mochi right about now.

00:35:10.080 --> 00:35:11.360
Yeah, no.

00:35:11.360 --> 00:35:12.480
Cheapskate.

00:35:12.480 --> 00:35:14.340
Cheapy, cheapy skate.

00:35:14.340 --> 00:35:16.220
Skaty cheap, cheap.

00:35:16.220 --> 00:35:18.380
Skating cheaper!

00:35:18.380 --> 00:35:20.130
There’s the curry mix.

00:35:21.020 --> 00:35:22.970
There’s a lot of varieties…

00:35:23.350 --> 00:35:25.400
We have to get mild!

00:35:25.400 --> 00:35:27.060
Spicy for sure!

00:35:27.060 --> 00:35:29.780
If it’s spicy, you can’t even tell how it tastes!

00:35:29.780 --> 00:35:32.310
What kind of curry lacks spice? Heresy, I say!

00:35:32.310 --> 00:35:35.380
Chinatsu-chan, you want it mild too, right?

00:35:35.380 --> 00:35:39.300
Despite how she looks, Mirakurun sometimes has a drop of spice in her!

00:35:39.300 --> 00:35:42.120
Mirakurun has nothing to do with this.

00:35:42.120 --> 00:35:43.940
Fine, let’s get the potato chips then.

00:35:43.940 --> 00:35:45.660
That has even less to do with this.

00:35:45.660 --> 00:35:48.260
A post-meal snack is important!

00:35:48.260 --> 00:35:50.620
This girl gets it!

00:35:50.620 --> 00:35:52.260
Where would we be without potato flavored chips?

00:35:52.260 --> 00:35:53.420
Where indeed!

00:35:53.420 --> 00:35:56.380
And the two of you were disagreeing just then…

00:35:56.380 --> 00:35:58.820
Everything goes well with miso flavor!

00:35:58.820 --> 00:36:01.010
Miso? You must mean mentaiko!

00:36:01.010 --> 00:36:03.220
Mentaiko? No way!

00:36:03.220 --> 00:36:05.320
Miso flavor is heresy!

00:36:05.320 --> 00:36:06.500
Mentaiko! Mentaiko! Mentaiko!

00:36:06.500 --> 00:36:09.760
Could you please stop fighting?!
Mentaiko! Mentaiko! Mentaiko!

00:36:12.660 --> 00:36:15.640
We’ll cook the rice al dente.

00:36:16.680 --> 00:36:18.150
I think that’s good.

00:36:18.150 --> 00:36:19.640
How are you doing there?

00:36:19.640 --> 00:36:22.110
I’ve just finished the preparations.

00:36:22.110 --> 00:36:24.500
Nice job. You’re good at this.

00:36:24.500 --> 00:36:26.180
Thank you.

00:36:28.180 --> 00:36:29.780
Funami-senpai?

00:36:29.780 --> 00:36:34.080
I just thought to myself,
things are almost going... <i>too</i>  smoothly.

00:36:34.080 --> 00:36:36.560
Ah, I think I understand.

00:36:40.670 --> 00:36:44.430
Were we using eggs for something?

00:36:45.940 --> 00:36:47.720
Would you like some help?

00:36:47.720 --> 00:36:52.100
Oh! No. It’s okay now. Thanks.

00:36:54.350 --> 00:36:57.320
Don’t put in too much.

00:36:57.320 --> 00:37:01.220
Watch: the flow of air is important.

00:37:01.220 --> 00:37:04.480
Wow, amazing! The flames are swelling!

00:37:05.380 --> 00:37:08.580
It’s like you know everything.

00:37:08.580 --> 00:37:11.980
No, I wouldn’t say that.

00:37:11.980 --> 00:37:15.340
But I do like to think about all kinds of things.

00:37:15.340 --> 00:37:16.680
All kinds of things?

00:37:19.450 --> 00:37:24.760
<i>Come to think of it, she seems to get nosebleeds pretty often. I wonder why?</i>

00:37:25.320 --> 00:37:30.420
Um, why is it that you often get nosebleeds?

00:37:30.420 --> 00:37:33.400
It happens when my fantasies are running loose.

00:37:33.400 --> 00:37:34.840
Fantasies?

00:37:35.640 --> 00:37:38.080
Well, you know…

00:37:38.080 --> 00:37:41.240
For example, if this was a campfire…

00:37:45.200 --> 00:37:46.960
Are you cold?

00:37:46.960 --> 00:37:49.800
I’m fine thanks to you.

00:37:49.800 --> 00:37:51.080
Are you afraid?

00:37:51.080 --> 00:37:54.180
I’m not afraid because you’re here with me.

00:37:56.290 --> 00:37:59.140
Let’s live on together, even if it’s only the two of us.

00:38:08.500 --> 00:38:12.680
This may be a little too early for you, Akaza-san.

00:38:12.680 --> 00:38:16.800
Come on! I’m a middle schooler now!

00:38:16.800 --> 00:38:22.790
That’s true. Well, imagine if two people did this with their hands.

00:38:22.790 --> 00:38:25.400
And then… uh…

00:38:26.280 --> 00:38:30.580
<i>If I try to put this in words… it’s actually really embarrassing!</i>

00:38:30.580 --> 00:38:36.660
<i>I had never thought of it,
but am I always thinking these crazy things?!</i>

00:38:36.660 --> 00:38:38.370
Ikeda-senpai?

00:38:38.370 --> 00:38:43.100
I-I’m sorry. I can’t say this after all. Just forget it.

00:38:43.100 --> 00:38:44.340
What?!

00:38:45.590 --> 00:38:49.280
<i>Yeah, I may be childish, but...</i>

00:38:49.280 --> 00:38:51.340
<i> I want to become more of an adult!</i>

00:38:51.340 --> 00:38:53.470
<i>I want to know about more things!</i>

00:38:56.060 --> 00:39:01.080
I may still be a child, but I want to hear what you have to say!

00:39:01.080 --> 00:39:03.200
Huh? No, that’s not—

00:39:03.200 --> 00:39:06.040
I want to become more of an adult, like you.

00:39:06.040 --> 00:39:07.820
Well, you see...

00:39:07.820 --> 00:39:08.990
Chitose!

00:39:08.990 --> 00:39:12.100
Can I put this on the flame for a bit?

00:39:12.100 --> 00:39:13.620
Oh, yeah! Of course.

00:39:13.620 --> 00:39:16.940
We just finished growing the fire.

00:39:16.940 --> 00:39:20.120
Akari, unless you’re busy could you lend us a hand over here?

00:39:20.120 --> 00:39:21.920
Okay!

00:39:21.920 --> 00:39:26.420
When I grow a little older, I want to hear all about it, okay?

00:39:26.420 --> 00:39:28.020
Well, here I go.

00:39:29.300 --> 00:39:31.300
What were you two talking about?

00:39:33.380 --> 00:39:36.220
N-Nothing at all…

00:39:39.750 --> 00:39:42.380
<i>What</i>  were <i>they talking about?!</i>

00:39:42.380 --> 00:39:44.270
Hey, everyone!

00:39:44.270 --> 00:39:46.680
‘Twas a bountiful catch!

00:39:57.240 --> 00:39:59.820
I think the flame is still a little too weak.

00:39:59.820 --> 00:40:03.800
I think Chitose had the fan. Let’s go get it.

00:40:05.340 --> 00:40:09.050
Leave this to your top idol Kyouko-chan!

00:40:09.050 --> 00:40:11.100
Who’s an idol now?

00:40:11.100 --> 00:40:12.260
A recorder?

00:40:12.260 --> 00:40:14.760
Using this, I will deliver air to the flame!

00:40:14.760 --> 00:40:17.640
Classic Kyouko-senpai! Gosh, she’s so smart.

00:40:18.620 --> 00:40:19.350
Here goes.

00:40:20.080 --> 00:40:21.500
One, two...!

00:40:24.980 --> 00:40:25.810
Try blowing.

00:40:25.810 --> 00:40:31.000
If you don’t plug all the holes, no way in Niagara will it work.

00:40:31.000 --> 00:40:33.820
Oh, oil! Let’s pour oil into the flame!

00:40:33.820 --> 00:40:35.820
Stop! That’s dangerous, you know?

00:40:40.220 --> 00:40:41.910
Is that Nishigaki-chan?

00:40:42.900 --> 00:40:45.760
Are those two… okay?

00:40:49.000 --> 00:40:51.340
Wow! This looks delicious!

00:40:51.340 --> 00:40:53.840
Curry a la Kyouko!

00:40:53.840 --> 00:40:55.960
You only bought the curry mix.

00:40:55.960 --> 00:41:00.620
Not just that. I picked out that curry mix.

00:41:00.620 --> 00:41:04.520
Yes, but half of it is Sakurako-chan’s mild mix.

00:41:04.520 --> 00:41:07.260
Did everybody get some?

00:41:07.260 --> 00:41:08.680
Yes!

00:41:08.680 --> 00:41:10.020
In that case:

00:41:10.020 --> 00:41:11.780
Let’s eat!

00:41:16.120 --> 00:41:17.450
Oh, this is good.

00:41:17.450 --> 00:41:18.860
Yeah, it is.

00:41:21.160 --> 00:41:24.800
Do you like it? Is it good? My curry?

00:41:24.800 --> 00:41:27.040
This isn’t your curry.

00:41:28.760 --> 00:41:30.200
It is good.

00:41:30.200 --> 00:41:31.600
Really?!

00:41:31.600 --> 00:41:34.420
Yeah. Thanks for going to the store.

00:41:34.420 --> 00:41:37.200
Then, you can have this carrot.

00:41:39.140 --> 00:41:40.140
Is it good?

00:41:40.960 --> 00:41:44.960
Yes. In return, you may have these bell peppers.

00:41:48.140 --> 00:41:49.520
Isn’t it good?

00:41:49.520 --> 00:41:52.820
After all, I’m not a child like you, Himawari.

00:41:52.820 --> 00:41:56.480
I don’t want to hear that from you when you can’t eat carrots.

00:41:56.480 --> 00:41:59.430
Well, carrots are for adults!

00:41:59.430 --> 00:42:01.390
They ought to give it only to people over 15.

00:42:01.390 --> 00:42:06.920
Then I’ll be sure to give you tons of carrots on your 15th birthday.

00:42:06.920 --> 00:42:11.120
No! I don’t want it!

00:42:17.300 --> 00:42:21.120
Himawari-oneechan has gone camping.

00:42:21.120 --> 00:42:23.270
Apparently they’re going to have curry together.

00:42:23.270 --> 00:42:29.940
I am worried that Sakurako-oneechan might have eaten too much.

00:42:33.820 --> 00:42:36.150
I can’t eat any more…

00:42:36.150 --> 00:42:42.000
I was finally able to say it.

00:42:42.000 --> 00:42:44.540
Good for you. You’ve accomplished your dream.

00:42:44.540 --> 00:42:47.340
My stomach is full to bursting.

00:42:47.340 --> 00:42:49.120
Congratulations.

00:42:52.140 --> 00:42:53.800
What are you doing?

00:42:53.800 --> 00:42:56.210
I thought maybe it’d help.

00:42:56.210 --> 00:42:58.470
You really ate a lot.

00:42:58.470 --> 00:43:01.850
We’re not out of the woods yet! There’s still dessert.

00:43:03.480 --> 00:43:04.500
What is it?

00:43:05.200 --> 00:43:07.400
Looks like she has something.

00:43:07.400 --> 00:43:08.860
Chitose…

00:43:08.860 --> 00:43:11.860
The Kyouko-chan is open to anything and everything!

00:43:12.320 --> 00:43:14.070
I suppose I have no choice.

00:43:22.660 --> 00:43:23.840
A cooking set?

00:43:29.080 --> 00:43:29.790
Pudding!

00:43:29.960 --> 00:43:30.790
Pudding?!

00:43:30.790 --> 00:43:33.940
Oh, so that’s what those eggs were for.

00:43:33.940 --> 00:43:36.220
It’s big! Amazing!

00:43:36.220 --> 00:43:37.580
That looks delicious.

00:43:37.580 --> 00:43:41.820
I wanted to eat some and I just happened to make a little too much, is all.

00:43:41.820 --> 00:43:44.000
Ayano, thank you!

00:43:44.880 --> 00:43:46.970
Sugiura-senpai, I love you!

00:43:46.970 --> 00:43:48.700
Me too!

00:43:48.700 --> 00:43:52.460
Quit it, you two...!

00:43:52.460 --> 00:43:54.340
Sheesh.

00:43:56.000 --> 00:43:58.020
Someone get tissues!

00:44:02.110 --> 00:44:04.070
Wow! Look at that!

00:44:04.070 --> 00:44:06.180
The stars are so clear!

00:44:06.180 --> 00:44:08.790
You’re right! They’re beautiful.

00:44:10.020 --> 00:44:12.000
Camping, and a clear night sky.

00:44:12.000 --> 00:44:15.250
When it comes to this, there’s only one thing to do.

00:44:15.250 --> 00:44:18.460
One thing? You mean…

00:44:18.460 --> 00:44:19.600
I’m too young!

00:44:19.600 --> 00:44:20.950
Probably not that.

00:44:20.950 --> 00:44:22.920
Homework…?

00:44:22.920 --> 00:44:23.840
Nope.

00:44:23.840 --> 00:44:25.850
Bathing? Brushing teeth?

00:44:25.850 --> 00:44:27.810
Hmm, no.

00:44:27.810 --> 00:44:31.020
We put on masks, grab chainsaws, and chase couples!

00:44:31.020 --> 00:44:32.940
What is this, a horror movie?

00:44:32.940 --> 00:44:34.940
And why would we be the ones doing the chasing?

00:44:34.940 --> 00:44:38.230
Summer is all about horror. It keeps you cool.

00:44:38.230 --> 00:44:40.190
A test of courage!

00:44:40.190 --> 00:44:41.600
Test of courage?

00:44:41.600 --> 00:44:43.620
Oomuro-san has the answer.

00:44:43.620 --> 00:44:46.760
Come on, Chitose…
Why do you have to bring up weird ideas?

00:44:46.760 --> 00:44:49.160
Doesn’t it sound like fun?

00:44:50.120 --> 00:44:52.870
<i>No way I’m going to miss this…</i>

00:44:55.350 --> 00:44:56.420
Four

00:44:56.420 --> 00:44:58.250
Oh, it’s Laika-chan!
Four

00:44:58.250 --> 00:45:00.940
Looks like I’m with you, Akari-chan.

00:45:00.940 --> 00:45:02.480
Let’s go together!

00:45:02.480 --> 00:45:03.260
Yeah!

00:45:03.260 --> 00:45:05.600
It looks like you’re my partner, Ayano.

00:45:05.600 --> 00:45:07.040
Let’s do our best!

00:45:07.040 --> 00:45:09.510
If that’s the result of the draw,
then I suppose there’s no other choice.

00:45:09.510 --> 00:45:10.940
Glad to work with you.

00:45:10.940 --> 00:45:12.140
Same here.

00:45:13.900 --> 00:45:15.820
You again?

00:45:15.820 --> 00:45:17.960
That’s my line.

00:45:17.960 --> 00:45:19.200
What did you say?

00:45:19.200 --> 00:45:20.230
What’s your problem?

00:45:20.230 --> 00:45:24.540
Careful, the frisky couple is always the first to die.

00:45:24.540 --> 00:45:27.080
We are not a frisky couple!

00:45:27.080 --> 00:45:29.240
That’s the part you’re concerned with?

00:45:33.680 --> 00:45:37.460
Kyouko solicited you to come camping with us out of nowhere, didn’t she?

00:45:37.460 --> 00:45:39.080
Was it bothersome?

00:45:39.080 --> 00:45:42.220
Not at all! It’s been a lot of fun.

00:45:42.220 --> 00:45:44.320
What about Chizuru, by the way?

00:45:44.320 --> 00:45:47.580
She prefers to stay home, apparently.

00:45:47.580 --> 00:45:48.180
Is that so?

00:45:48.180 --> 00:45:51.560
Next time, though, it’d be nice if she could come.

00:45:51.560 --> 00:45:56.350
Really? She’s very shy, but I’m sure she’d love it.

00:46:02.250 --> 00:46:04.520
Alright. We made it.

00:46:04.520 --> 00:46:06.860
That was pretty quick.

00:46:06.860 --> 00:46:08.460
Let’s go back, then.

00:46:08.460 --> 00:46:10.640
It was this way, right?

00:46:10.640 --> 00:46:11.360
Yeah.

00:46:15.680 --> 00:46:20.160
What should I do… I’m not good with the dark…

00:46:20.160 --> 00:46:23.160
Afraid of the dark? You’re such a baby!

00:46:23.160 --> 00:46:24.550
What did you say?

00:46:24.550 --> 00:46:29.260
<i>To be honest, when she’s like this I feel like I can rely on her.</i>

00:46:35.080 --> 00:46:37.400
I’m not scared! I’m not scared! I’m not scared!

00:46:37.400 --> 00:46:40.320
S-Sakurako…?

00:46:40.320 --> 00:46:42.360
Oh, come on…

00:46:56.200 --> 00:46:57.180
What’s the matter?

00:47:00.120 --> 00:47:02.920
It’s so quiet, I can’t concentrate.

00:47:09.090 --> 00:47:10.800
That was so freaky!

00:47:10.800 --> 00:47:15.460
I was fine with the dark, but then,
something horrible emerged from the shadows!

00:47:15.460 --> 00:47:19.660
Chinatsu-chan, would you rather be in front or behind?

00:47:22.460 --> 00:47:27.580
When you’re waiting to get your shots,

00:47:27.580 --> 00:47:30.200
are you the type to go first, or wait till last?

00:47:30.200 --> 00:47:33.450
F-First! Definitely first!

00:47:33.450 --> 00:47:39.320
Kyouko-chan, Sugiura-senpai… Can we go first?

00:47:39.320 --> 00:47:40.860
Sure, but...

00:47:40.860 --> 00:47:42.170
But… what?

00:47:42.600 --> 00:47:46.580
Didn’t you know?
Those who go second last are most likely to die!

00:47:47.570 --> 00:47:48.580
Quit it.

00:47:54.280 --> 00:47:57.560
Yeah… this is actually pretty scary.

00:47:57.560 --> 00:48:01.100
Akari-chan… don’t suddenly disappear on me or anything, okay?

00:48:02.340 --> 00:48:04.500
I’m not going to disappear.

00:48:04.500 --> 00:48:06.440
Are you really sure?

00:48:09.700 --> 00:48:10.570
Akari-chan.

00:48:10.570 --> 00:48:15.440
If you do disappear,
please at least leave behind your dotted outline.

00:48:15.440 --> 00:48:17.440
<i>What do you mean dotted outline?!</i>

00:48:22.370 --> 00:48:25.280
Akane-chan? It’s Yoshikawa.

00:48:26.800 --> 00:48:30.840
Yes, I heard from Chinatsu-chan that you’re alone in the house.

00:48:30.840 --> 00:48:32.600
Do you have anybody to keep you company?

00:48:32.600 --> 00:48:37.980
If… If it’s alright, could I possibly—!

00:48:37.980 --> 00:48:38.930
Thank you.

00:48:38.930 --> 00:48:42.390
But… I’m just fine!
...Sister
...x
Sister

00:48:42.390 --> 00:48:43.600
Sakurako!

00:48:43.600 --> 00:48:47.540
Do you understand what you just put me through?

00:48:47.540 --> 00:48:49.480
Hey! Listen when people are talking to you!

00:48:49.480 --> 00:48:52.530
Alright then. I guess it’s our turn now.

00:48:52.530 --> 00:48:54.440
Here we go!

00:48:54.900 --> 00:48:57.240
It’s like a child leaving to run an errand.

00:48:57.240 --> 00:49:01.160
Yeah. I wonder what they will talk about?

00:49:02.860 --> 00:49:04.780
Excuse me, I’m going to wash my hands.

00:49:05.900 --> 00:49:08.340
Yui-senpai!

00:49:08.340 --> 00:49:10.670
It was really, really scary!

00:49:10.670 --> 00:49:13.550
I didn’t know if I should just take off running or not,

00:49:13.550 --> 00:49:17.520
I returned here thinking of you!

00:49:25.380 --> 00:49:28.400
Could you say something?

00:49:31.450 --> 00:49:35.680
Alright then. There was once a place where an old man and his wife lived...

00:49:35.680 --> 00:49:36.740
Is this a folk tale?

00:49:36.740 --> 00:49:41.080
One night, they heard a knocking on their attic door.

00:49:41.080 --> 00:49:44.080
When the old lady opened the door, nobody was there.

00:49:44.080 --> 00:49:45.330
Hold on…

00:49:45.330 --> 00:49:47.620
Once again, there is knocking.

00:49:47.620 --> 00:49:49.740
This time, the old man came.

00:49:49.740 --> 00:49:53.710
The attic was completely soaked in water! And then…

00:49:53.710 --> 00:49:55.650
Stop! I’ve had enough!

00:49:55.650 --> 00:50:00.360
What? I was weaving an epic story for you there.

00:50:00.360 --> 00:50:04.010
Toshinou Kyouko, you’re not afraid? It’s dark here.

00:50:04.010 --> 00:50:08.060
Yeah! I love zombies and Dracula and all that good stuff.

00:50:08.060 --> 00:50:09.320
You’re a weird person.

00:50:09.320 --> 00:50:10.980
How about you, Ayano? What do you like?

00:50:10.980 --> 00:50:15.740
What? What do I like? Well, lots of things.

00:50:15.740 --> 00:50:17.420
Like Frankenstein?

00:50:17.420 --> 00:50:19.460
Stop fixating on horror.

00:50:19.460 --> 00:50:22.120
Me, I just like people.

00:50:22.120 --> 00:50:23.600
Really? Who?!

00:50:23.600 --> 00:50:26.200
Is it everybody’s favorite top idol Toshinou Kyouko-chan?

00:50:26.200 --> 00:50:28.200
Who’s an idol now?

00:50:28.200 --> 00:50:31.500
I mean like Chitose, the vice president and others like that.

00:50:31.500 --> 00:50:33.460
Chitose, huh? I see.

00:50:34.670 --> 00:50:39.350
That’s right! She’s serious about work,
and a considerate person on top of that.

00:50:39.350 --> 00:50:42.440
I see. That’s like me, almost.

00:50:43.540 --> 00:50:49.480
Anyway! She’s always such a helpful person, and I’m always indebted to her.

00:50:50.480 --> 00:50:54.200
And… you too, Toshinou Kyouko…

00:50:54.200 --> 00:50:55.580
Huh? What did you say?

00:50:55.580 --> 00:50:56.360
It’s nothing!

00:50:56.360 --> 00:50:58.800
What about me?

00:50:58.800 --> 00:51:00.440
You heard what I said!

00:51:00.440 --> 00:51:02.520
No, I didn’t hear!

00:51:02.520 --> 00:51:03.100
Liar!

00:51:03.100 --> 00:51:04.740
That’s why I’m asking!

00:51:20.220 --> 00:51:21.260
Kyouko-chan?

00:51:21.260 --> 00:51:22.840
What happened?

00:51:22.840 --> 00:51:24.580
Did you see a ghost?

00:51:24.580 --> 00:51:26.800
A severed head! All bloody!

00:51:41.320 --> 00:51:44.660
I thought my heart would stop!

00:51:44.660 --> 00:51:47.300
It was a real scare.

00:51:47.300 --> 00:51:48.370
So sorry.

00:51:48.370 --> 00:51:51.360
We really shed a lot of sweat.

00:51:51.360 --> 00:51:53.980
It’s a good thing there was a bath house nearby.

00:51:55.260 --> 00:51:58.380
I anticipated this! That’s why I chose this place.

00:51:58.380 --> 00:51:59.340
Yeah, great.

00:52:02.800 --> 00:52:04.300
This is spacious.

00:52:04.300 --> 00:52:07.640
Yay, bath time! I love bath time!

00:52:07.640 --> 00:52:09.600
There’s a lot of baths.

00:52:09.600 --> 00:52:11.960
I wonder which I’ll get in first.

00:52:11.960 --> 00:52:13.780
Oh wow! A jacuzzi!

00:52:13.780 --> 00:52:15.600
The open air bath is also a contender.

00:52:15.600 --> 00:52:16.810
And what’s over there?!

00:52:16.810 --> 00:52:19.770
Kyouko-chan! It’s dangerous to run!

00:52:38.220 --> 00:52:40.130
What do you think you’re doing?!

00:52:41.260 --> 00:52:42.900
It sure is lively.

00:52:42.900 --> 00:52:44.420
Really.

00:52:44.420 --> 00:52:47.140
You don’t mind being in the open air bath with me?

00:52:47.140 --> 00:52:50.140
Of course not. I feel calm with you around.

00:52:51.440 --> 00:52:53.850
Don’t say that, I’ll blubblubllb...

00:52:54.640 --> 00:53:00.400
Even my mother told me,
I’m really lucky to have a friend like you.

00:53:02.800 --> 00:53:04.140
Chitose?!

00:53:05.440 --> 00:53:09.680
I’m also glad that you’re my friend.

00:53:09.680 --> 00:53:11.140
Geronimo!

00:53:12.040 --> 00:53:12.930
Toshinou Kyouko!

00:53:12.930 --> 00:53:17.320
Make room, make room!
The Kyouko-chan has decided to join the party.

00:53:18.540 --> 00:53:20.420
There’s no helping it.

00:53:20.420 --> 00:53:23.620
Kyouko, show a little restraint, won’t you?

00:53:23.620 --> 00:53:26.740
It’s no problem. Would you like to get in too?

00:53:27.540 --> 00:53:28.680
Is there space?

00:53:28.680 --> 00:53:31.300
It’s fine.

00:53:31.300 --> 00:53:33.560
Well, I might as well then.

00:53:35.480 --> 00:53:38.320
It sure feels nice.

00:53:38.320 --> 00:53:39.860
Yeah, it does.

00:53:39.860 --> 00:53:42.200
And it’s all thanks to me!

00:53:42.200 --> 00:53:43.260
Yeah, yeah.

00:53:44.860 --> 00:53:47.540
What’s all this? Looks like fun!

00:53:48.000 --> 00:53:49.200
Fun?

00:53:49.200 --> 00:53:51.450
I get it! You’re trying to fit as many people as possible!

00:53:52.740 --> 00:53:55.660
Akari-chan! Chinatsu-chan!

00:53:55.660 --> 00:53:57.540
Sakurako-chan?

00:53:57.540 --> 00:53:59.140
What’s going on?

00:54:02.380 --> 00:54:06.090
We can still... still fit… more!

00:54:13.000 --> 00:54:14.300
That hit the spot!

00:54:15.580 --> 00:54:20.120
Now then, everybody. Let us now return to our castle!

00:54:22.080 --> 00:54:24.640
Akari-chan, is your head OK?

00:54:24.640 --> 00:54:28.160
Yeah… well actually it still hurts a bit.

00:54:28.160 --> 00:54:31.490
And to think that I specifically chose this bath house because I heard it heals bruises.

00:54:31.490 --> 00:54:33.720
I don’t think that would help...

00:54:36.820 --> 00:54:38.900
It’s starting to get cold.

00:54:38.900 --> 00:54:40.180
Did you bring something warm to wear?

00:54:40.180 --> 00:54:42.920
I only brought a hoodie in case it rains.

00:54:42.920 --> 00:54:44.120
Same here.

00:54:44.120 --> 00:54:45.880
Kyouko-chan to the rescue!

00:54:53.530 --> 00:54:55.440
These are pretty cute!

00:54:56.100 --> 00:54:57.490
These suit all of you pretty well.

00:54:57.490 --> 00:55:00.980
It’s a bit embarrassing though…

00:55:00.980 --> 00:55:05.940
Yeah. After all, you’re not cute enough to be a rabbit.

00:55:05.940 --> 00:55:08.660
Well, yours suits you just fine.

00:55:08.660 --> 00:55:10.440
Oh? Well!

00:55:10.440 --> 00:55:12.940
Yes, in that you have a memory span of three steps.

00:55:12.940 --> 00:55:14.860
Huh? Did you say something?

00:55:14.860 --> 00:55:16.450
Oh, nothing.

00:55:16.450 --> 00:55:19.800
You went to all the trouble of bringing these?

00:55:19.800 --> 00:55:21.430
Thanks so much, Toshinou-san!

00:55:21.430 --> 00:55:23.700
There’s no need to thank me.

00:55:23.700 --> 00:55:24.820
Who are you?

00:55:24.820 --> 00:55:26.020
Oops, wrong outfit.

00:55:26.760 --> 00:55:28.400
That’s more like it.

00:55:28.400 --> 00:55:30.590
That’s way too forced.

00:55:30.590 --> 00:55:33.300
No, the proper thing to say in that situation was “Kyouko-chan is so cute!”

00:55:33.300 --> 00:55:34.700
Or something like that.

00:55:34.700 --> 00:55:37.140
Yeah, alright. “Kyouko-chan is so cute.”

00:55:37.140 --> 00:55:38.990
Hey. Ayano is cute too!

00:55:38.990 --> 00:55:40.640
C-C—

00:55:40.640 --> 00:55:44.360
I’m wearing it only because I had to!

00:55:44.360 --> 00:55:45.730
That’s too bad. It’s really cute.

00:55:45.730 --> 00:55:48.690
But if it’s such a bother, you don’t have to.

00:55:48.690 --> 00:55:50.540
Huh? Well...

00:55:51.660 --> 00:55:53.760
I guess it’s fine since I don’t have anything else as warm.

00:55:53.760 --> 00:55:56.130
I <i>sheepose</i>  I’ll take you up on your offer.

00:55:56.130 --> 00:55:57.560
Thanks.

00:55:57.560 --> 00:55:59.560
Really? I’m glad.

00:56:02.860 --> 00:56:06.420
Akari-chan? Are you feeling sleepy?

00:56:07.960 --> 00:56:09.780
I’m fine.

00:56:10.880 --> 00:56:16.240
I want to talk with you guys more…

00:56:16.740 --> 00:56:19.240
But you look really sleepy.

00:56:19.240 --> 00:56:23.080
Don’t worry. I’m widely awake.

00:56:23.430 --> 00:56:26.390
Today was… really…

00:56:27.160 --> 00:56:30.250
You’re falling asleep! Akari-chan!

00:56:31.400 --> 00:56:33.340
Well then, good night.

00:56:33.340 --> 00:56:35.340
Good night!

00:56:39.600 --> 00:56:43.620
There was supposed to be a hill with a great view around here. I forgot!

00:56:43.620 --> 00:56:45.380
I guess we’ll do that tomorrow.

00:56:45.380 --> 00:56:46.980
I’m looking forward to it.

00:56:46.980 --> 00:56:48.090
Darn.

00:57:09.580 --> 00:57:12.060
Morning, Akaza-san.

00:57:12.060 --> 00:57:15.340
Sugiura-senpai! Good morning.

00:57:18.300 --> 00:57:19.060
Here you go.

00:57:19.060 --> 00:57:20.600
Thank you!

00:57:20.600 --> 00:57:21.780
You’re up early.

00:57:21.780 --> 00:57:24.140
I just woke up for some reason.

00:57:24.140 --> 00:57:25.560
Me too.

00:57:25.560 --> 00:57:29.740
It’s still early, but why don’t we start making breakfast?

00:57:29.740 --> 00:57:31.350
Yes. I’ll help.

00:57:40.400 --> 00:57:42.320
A sheep and a dog.

00:57:42.960 --> 00:57:44.300
Is this a farm?

00:57:48.400 --> 00:57:49.730
Good morning!

00:57:50.820 --> 00:57:52.400
Morning.

00:57:52.400 --> 00:57:53.940
A little longer…

00:57:53.940 --> 00:57:57.980
The fish is in the tiger’s jaws…

00:58:01.340 --> 00:58:04.120
Oh, she’s always bad with waking up.

00:58:04.120 --> 00:58:06.330
All the blood is being redirected to her boobs and all.

00:58:13.360 --> 00:58:14.190
Kiss...

00:58:28.320 --> 00:58:30.020
Wow! Look!

00:58:44.620 --> 00:58:46.020
Amazing!

00:58:50.480 --> 00:58:52.020
Beautiful.

00:59:17.100 --> 00:59:21.460
I’m so happy to be with everybody.

00:59:29.120 --> 00:59:32.060
This is such a wonderful summer vaca—<i>chuu</i> !

00:59:36.790 --> 00:59:41.080
Come on, Akari. You messed it up.

00:59:54.330 --> 01:00:01.640
There’s a saying: “Take nothing but photographs, and leave nothing but footsteps.”

01:00:01.640 --> 01:00:03.070
Get to work.

01:00:07.300 --> 01:00:08.760
You’re alright?

01:00:08.760 --> 01:00:11.850
Yeah. We decided we’re all going back together.

01:00:11.850 --> 01:00:15.400
In that case, we’ll take all your luggage back to the school.

01:00:15.400 --> 01:00:17.730
Yay! Nothing to carry!
Thank you very much.

01:00:21.730 --> 01:00:23.410
Take care!

01:00:23.410 --> 01:00:25.580
Especially the explosions!

01:00:26.900 --> 01:00:29.700
Okay, now let’s go home.

01:00:29.700 --> 01:00:30.880
Yeah.

01:00:30.880 --> 01:00:33.400
The bus is this way, right?

01:00:33.400 --> 01:00:34.700
That’s right.

01:00:34.700 --> 01:00:37.540
Sakurako actually knew the right direction?

01:00:37.540 --> 01:00:39.620
Oomuro-san, are you good with maps?

01:00:39.620 --> 01:00:39.840
Not at all! My sense of direction is all it takes!

01:00:39.840 --> 01:00:41.840
Not at all! My sense of direction is all it takes!

01:00:41.840 --> 01:00:43.620
Not at all! My sense of direction is all it takes!

01:00:47.360 --> 01:00:50.440
Akari-chan! What’s the matter?

01:00:50.440 --> 01:00:52.700
No, it’s nothing!

01:01:03.900 --> 01:01:10.400
One day, we’ll come back together!

01:01:11.260 --> 01:01:12.360
Well I’ll be.

01:01:12.360 --> 01:01:17.820
We could’ve just skipped the train and took a bus straight here.

01:01:17.820 --> 01:01:20.640
Somebody really wanted to ride that Mirakurun train.

01:01:20.640 --> 01:01:23.800
Hey, who cares! It was fun.

01:01:23.800 --> 01:01:25.760
Yeah, it was!

01:01:25.760 --> 01:01:28.400
You’re really a handful, Kyouko.

01:01:28.400 --> 01:01:30.880
That’s really like Kyouko-senpai.

01:01:30.880 --> 01:01:33.200
Oh, the bus is here.

01:01:44.820 --> 01:01:47.240
I wonder when we’ll be able to come back.

01:01:47.240 --> 01:01:48.660
Soon, I bet!

01:01:48.660 --> 01:01:49.530
Definitely.

01:01:49.530 --> 01:01:50.960
Yeah!

01:01:51.780 --> 01:01:53.030
Like tomorrow, or something.

01:01:54.200 --> 01:01:56.860
What do you think you’re saying, Toshinou Kyouko?

01:01:56.860 --> 01:01:58.060
That’s a bit too early.

01:01:58.060 --> 01:02:00.640
Now that we’ve been to the mountains,
naturally the sea is next our destination!

01:02:00.640 --> 01:02:03.760
Sakurako, you’d better finish up your homework first.

01:02:04.740 --> 01:02:07.400
Oh, isn’t there going to be a festival too?

01:02:07.400 --> 01:02:10.360
Oh! I want to go to the amusement park!

01:02:10.360 --> 01:02:18.080
Oh jeez! I’m looking forward to so many things!

01:02:30.020 --> 01:02:32.640
kyou wa tsukkomi, ashita wa boke de
You’re stuck somewhere between serious and playful,

01:02:32.640 --> 01:02:35.050
nanda ka hen na kanji
somehow it just doesn’t feel right.

01:02:35.050 --> 01:02:37.840
narenai koto de bimyou na kanji
It’s hard to get used to, and sometimes it’s a bother,

01:02:37.840 --> 01:02:40.180
tsukarecchau kedo
it just really tires you out.

01:02:40.180 --> 01:02:45.350
tokidoki kawaru koto de atarashii hakken
But if you change something, you just might see,

01:02:45.350 --> 01:02:50.770
mainichi ga totemo shinsen, wakuwaku tomaranai
that each day can be fresh, and full of adventure.

01:02:50.770 --> 01:02:53.500
egao ga mitai yo
I wanna see your smile

01:02:53.500 --> 01:02:56.140
hengao mo ii ne
or at least your silly face.

01:02:56.140 --> 01:03:01.240
minna no kao ga itsudemo daisuki yo
Seeing your smiles always brings me joy.

01:03:01.240 --> 01:03:03.980
kawaiku waratte
Give me a cute smile.

01:03:03.980 --> 01:03:06.060
minna de piisu yo
everyone, let’s PEACE.

01:03:06.060 --> 01:03:08.710
kono shunkan wo nokoshitai kara
I wanna hold onto this moment,

01:03:08.710 --> 01:03:14.090
watashitachi no memorii hyakubai fuyashitai yo
so let’s relive it again, a hundred times over.

01:03:14.090 --> 01:03:15.970
One, two, three, four, let’s go!

01:03:15.970 --> 01:03:20.320
sora ni kakaru kono niji wo miagetara
Just look up at this rainbow stretching into the sky,

01:03:20.320 --> 01:03:27.060
mune no oku e to kimochi ii kaze tsukinukeru yo
and a wonderful breeze will touch your heart.

01:03:27.060 --> 01:03:32.980
kagayaku kono sekai de itsumo hanashite kureru
You can always find someone

01:03:32.980 --> 01:03:37.240
taisetsu na mono wakaru you ni
who’ll remind you what matters in this one world.

01:03:37.240 --> 01:03:37.320
who’ll remind you what matters in this one world.

01:03:37.320 --> 01:03:42.370
itsumademo tsudzuku yo, minna shiawase da mon
These times won’t end, as long as we keep looking up

01:03:42.370 --> 01:03:48.080
daisuki na SLOW & LOVE
I love you all! Slow & Love!

01:03:49.050 --> 01:03:54.760
The End
